{{nihongo|The '''Hyōgo Prefectural Museum of Art'''|兵庫県立美術館|Hyōgo Kenritsu Bijutsukan}} is a purpose built municipal [[art museum|art gallery]] in [[Nada-ku, Kobe|Nada-ku]], [[Kobe]], [[Hyōgo Prefecture]], [[Japan]]. It was opened in 2002.

The major collections of the museum are foreign and Japanese [[sculpture]]s, foreign and Japanese [[printmaking|prints]], Western-style and [[Nihonga|Japanese-style]] [[painting]]s associated with Hyogo Prefecture, Japanese greatworks in modern era, and [[contemporary art]].

The museum has rooms dedicated to [[Ryōhei Koiso]] and [[Kanayama Heizō]], two significant Japanese modernist artists trained in the [[Art of Europe|European tradition]].

The museum building was designed by Japanese [[architect]] [[Tadao Ando]], whose Tadao Ando Architectural Institute undertook the design and construction costs, after which the building was donated to the prefecture.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2019-05-29 |title=兵庫県立美術館に安藤忠雄さんのギャラリー開館 |url=https://artexhibition.jp/topics/news/20190529-AEJ82260/ |access-date=2023-11-26 |website=美術展ナビ |language=ja |archive-date=2020-09-23 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200923160244/https://artexhibition.jp/topics/news/20190529-AEJ82260/ |url-status=dead }}</ref>

